{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"The literature supports the requested concept: TSCM are described as long-lived, naïve-like memory T cells with self-renewal and multipotent differentiation capacity that can regenerate central and effector memory subsets. I’m now building the actual axioms, keeping the modeling conservative: explicit parentage plus issue/provenance annotations, without overcommitting to species-specific marker restrictions that the issue thread itself flags as a broader follow-up."}}
